WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.330
Few heroes in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
have been as fun to follow over the years

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:04.900
as the Hulk.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.580
From his perpetual inner conflict to his temper,
nearly limitless strength, and near invincibility,

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.300
the character has plotted a uniquely absorbing
story that few of his fellow heroes can match.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.820
Here's his story in full.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.360
While you can find "the beginning" for most
MCU heroes simply by heading back to their

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.790
origin stories, the earliest moments of the
Hulk's timeline are a little harder to pin

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.280
down.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.100
The problem is, Hulk technically doesn't have
an MCU origin story like he does in other

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.600
movies.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.140
Not in detail, anyway.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.000
In fact, his story begins several years after
the "Other Guy" already came into existence.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.079
However, over time and through hints, exposition,
and flashbacks, it becomes clear that Banner

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:47.710
originally volunteered to test his own gamma
radiation experiment on himself, and things

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.240
quickly went very wrong.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.530
The experiment led to the creation of the
Hulk, a being that, in simplistic terms, shares

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.360
a body and mind with Bruce Banner — although
for many years, only one could express themselves

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.440
at any one time.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.080
Not long after the accident, the duo find
themselves on the lam.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.340
These early years are rough for Banner, who
is constantly tracked by the U.S. Army.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.140
He struggles to contain the Hulk in order
to stay quiet and out of sight.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.640
After several years of moving around, the
scientist finds himself living a secret life

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:21.030
as a fugitive in Brazil, where he focuses
on anger management and searches for ways

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.180
to reverse his "condition."

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.220
"You don't understand!

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.940
Something really bad is about to happen here!"

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.020
By 2008, Banner has spent nearly half a year
hiding in Brazil, where he works in a bottling

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:30.520
factory.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.440
However, his tenuous situation is upended
when General "Thunderbolt" Ross finally tracks

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:35.940
him down.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.640
When this happens, he transforms into the
Hulk, blows his cover, and goes back on the

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.140
run.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.970
The ensuing adventure sees Banner return to
America, where he reunites with his sweetheart,

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.700
the general's daughter Betty Ross, and continues
his quest to "heal" himself of his condition.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.440
Throughout these events, he's closely dogged
by General Ross' forces, and even meets them

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.380
head-on in front of Culver University — where
he is directly confronted by Emil Blonsky,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.351
a British special-ops commando injected with
a Super Soldier Serum that allows him to survive

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.940
his first encounter with the Hulk.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.940
After that, Blonsky escalates the situation
by having the Hulk's blood transfused into

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.180
his own body, an event that turns him into
the Hulk-sized villain Abomination.

00:02:16.529 --> 00:02:20.860
Meanwhile, Banner realizes the futility of
trying to fix his condition and is finally

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.740
taken into custody by General Ross — just
in time for Abomination to appear on the scene.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.939
This new threat forces Ross to release Banner,
as it quickly becomes apparent that Hulk is

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.460
the only hope they have to contain the transformed
Blonsky.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.900
This leads to a catastrophic showdown in Harlem,
where Abomination is subdued and Hulk flees

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.400
the scene.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:43.820
After the events in Harlem, it seems apparent
that the scientist may finally be gaining

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.640
a level of control over his angrier other
half.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.980
However, by the time he re-enters the larger
MCU story, much of that progress has been

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.480
lost, and the scientist is once again living
a quiet life of solitude — this time hiding

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.860
in India and helping the local population.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.980
It's here that Black Widow pays him a visit
in 2012, asking him to lend his impressive

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:08.200
scientific knowledge to SHIELD in its attempt
to find the Tesseract and protect the world

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.540
from a global threat.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:13.960
Banner reluctantly agrees, and soon finds
himself working alongside the crew that will

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.360
soon be known to the world as the Avengers.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.900
Although Banner joins the team with good intentions,
it doesn't take long for the Hulk to show

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.980
up and threaten the entire operation.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.719
After a tussle with Thor that almost destroys
S.H.I.E.L.D.'s Helicarrier, Hulk ends up falling

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.760
out of the sky, before turning back into Banner
on the ground.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.980
From there, he's given a helping hand by a
security guard, who lends him his motorcycle

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.460
so he can reunite with the team.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.239
When Banner reunites with the Avengers, they're
in the early stages of fending off an invasion

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.040
of Chitauri soldiers on the streets of New
York City.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.060
As he heads into battle, he reveals the one
thing that has taught him how to willingly

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.280
control his transformations into the Hulk.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.280
"That's my secret, Cap.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.260
I'm always angry."

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.139
The Hulk plays a central role in the ensuing
Battle of New York, smashing Chitauri, stopping

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.060
a leviathan or two, and even giving Loki a
particularly brutal smackdown in Stark Tower.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.420
After the battle, Banner finds that he no
longer needs to live perpetually in fear of

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.440
arrest, and settles into a new phase of his
superhero career.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:21.060
At one point, he even attempts to help Tony
Stark process some of the reformed playboy's

00:04:21.069 --> 00:04:22.230
own traumatic experiences.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.470
"You were actively napping?"

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.520
"I was..I...I drifted."

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.600
Over the next few years, Banner and Hulk continue
to work with the Avengers, albeit in two very

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.360
different capacities — Banner as the brains
and Hulk as the brawn.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:40.600
Prior to the Battle of Sokovia, Banner continues
to offer the Avengers his incredible intellect

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.710
as a scientist.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.199
He helps Tony Stark work on combining Baron
Von Strucker's work with the Ultron program

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.810
— inadvertently creating Ultron in the process.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:53.620
He also helps create Vision, and even strikes
up a romantic spark with Natasha Romanoff.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.750
Hulk, on the other hand, is repeatedly brought
out to "save the day" when the team is in

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.540
a tight spot.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:03.700
This begins with the retrieval of Loki's Scepter
from Von Strucker's base in Sokovia and ends

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.900
with the world-saving showdown with Ultron
in the same location.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.960
In the interim, he also duels Iron Man in
Johannesburg, reinforcing the troubling truth

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.280
that the Green Machine is little more than
an unwieldy tool in the hands of his fellow

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.420
Once Ultron is defeated, the Hulk refuses
to surrender control back to Banner, instead

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.520
taking the Avengers' Quinjet and flying off
into the unknown.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.960
After the events of Sokovia, Hulk's story
takes a rather dramatic turn.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:33.140
While flying the Quinjet through space, the
Hulk enters a wormhole and suddenly finds

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.840
himself crash-landing on the strange garbage
planet known as Sakaar.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:41.960
Once there, his powerful physique and fighting
prowess catches the attention of the the Grandmaster,

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.860
who recruits him as one of his gladiators
— a position uniquely suited to Hulk's violence-prone

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:47.360
temperament.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.560
Hulk remains in control for the next two Earth
years.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:56.259
It isn't until 2017 that the cover is finally
blown on his self-imposed exile when he finds

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.880
himself confronted in gladiatorial combat
by none other than his fellow Avenger, Thor.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.320
After a hotly-contested duel in the Grandmaster's
arena, the pair retire to Hulk's private quarters

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.120
where they discuss what to do next.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.020
"We must prevent Ragnarok"

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:21.560
While Hulk has no desire to leave his comfy
situation, he does show Thor where the Quinjet

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:25.610
landed, which inadvertently exposes him to
a recording of Black Widow — and allows

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.660
Banner to regain control of his mind.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:32.860
Once Banner is back, he and Thor join with
Valkyrie and Loki to form the Revengers and

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.120
head back to Asgard.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:39.000
There, Banner and Hulk help Thor stop his
villainous sister Hela by unleashing Ragnarok.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:44.060
During the fight, Hulk fearlessly dispatches
Hela's giant wolf Fenris and then jumps right

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:47.960
into the maw of the fiery Surtur while the
monster is in the middle of destroying Asgard.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:53.199
Afterward, Hulk joins the surviving Asgardians
as they evacuate onto a spaceship just in

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.320
time to escape Asgard's destruction.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:07:00.080
With Thor's home reduced to atoms behind them,
they set a course for Earth — only to be

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.700
intercepted by Thanos, who destroys the ship
and kills most of the passengers.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:09.039
When Hulk attempts to stop him, the Mad Titan
decisively wins their fight with a few well-placed

00:07:09.039 --> 00:07:13.800
blows, and Hulk is only saved from death when
Heimdall summons the Bifrost and sends him

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.860
hurtling back to Earth.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.100
This disastrous confrontation is the final
straw for Hulk, who refuses to help the Avengers

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.680
in the ensuing conflict with Thanos and his
armies.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:27.000
Instead, Banner is left to do his level best
with Tony Stark's Hulkbuster armor.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.039
While Hulk's absence comes across as cowardice
on the surface, his motivation is at least

00:07:32.039 --> 00:07:36.289
partly fueled by the fact that he refuses
to be taken advantage of by the Avengers all

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.100
over again.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.840
Hulk's absence from the first round of the
war against Thanos serves as a crisis point

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:42.360
for the hero.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.620
And while it initially has catastrophic consequences,
it ultimately leads Banner to the next step

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.920
in his story's evolution.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.660
During the five years after Thanos snaps away
half of the universe, Banner and Hulk finally

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.860
confront one another in an attempt to find
some kind of middle ground.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.640
The result: Professor Hulk.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.540
Realizing that he needs to stop seeing Hulk
as a problem, Banner decides to embrace his

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.789
alter ego as "the cure" to his maladies.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:11.040
He dives back into his long-dormant gamma
radiation research and spends 18 months in

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.080
a lab, fusing his own consciousness and intellect
with Hulk's physical prowess.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:19.800
This new round of experiments officially brings
the two-sided character together into one

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.160
personality for the first time in the MCU.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:27.420
The arrival of Professor Hulk ends up transforming
not only the character but also his role within

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:28.640
the MCU.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:34.080
The cerebral yet musclebound hero finds a
new lease on life by the time 2023 rolls around,

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.440
as he helps the Avengers turn back the clock
and undo the damage of Thanos' snap.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.920
First, he's brought in by Captain America,
Black Widow, and Ant-Man to help figure out

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.840
time travel during Tony Stark's temporary
retirement.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:50.750
While that experiment ends up a flop, it doesn't
change the fact that the green-skinned Avenger

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:55.580
still knows enough to properly and concisely
explain how time travel in the MCU works.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:09.610
Next, he time travels back to New York City
in 2012, where he is faced with the embarrassment

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.380
of encountering his past self.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.240
From there, he's able to find the Ancient
One and convince her to surrender her most

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.240
prized possession: the Time Stone.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:21.860
After the team has traveled through time and
gathered the six Infinity Stones, they return

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.050
to the Avengers Headquarters in Upstate New
York in order to officially assemble Stark's

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:27.480
version of the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.520
Once that gauntlet is complete, though, one
question remains: who will put it on and snap

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:33.520
their fingers?

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.640
"Let me do it.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.800
Just let me do something right."

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:43.780
Ultimately it's Hulk who steps up, declaring
that his resilience to gamma radiation makes

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.640
him the perfect candidate for the job.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:50.100
He dons the gauntlet and snaps his fingers,
restoring half of the universe in an instant

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.120
— and causing permanent damage to his arm
in the process.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:57.960
This move is indicative of how far the character
has come since those early days of inner turmoil,

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:00.040
hot tempers, and childish behavior.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:04.320
At the end of the day, it's Hulk that makes
the sacrifice play, and brings back half of

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.860
the universe in the process.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.860
While his arm took some serious damage from
undoing Thanos' snap, Hulk is hardly down

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.560
for the count.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:16.720
On the contrary, Hulk is one of the only original
Avengers still standing post-Endgame, which

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.220
means his future in the MCU is wide open.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.060
Not only is he in an excellent place as far
as his personal story arc goes, but he's also

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:28.290
a character that has spent time on and off
Earth, which means he could join with anyone

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:32.470
from Spider-Man in the Big Apple to Captain
Marvel on Hala or even the Guardians of the

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.360
Galaxy as they search for Gamora.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:39.340
According to CheatSheet, Hulk actor Mark Ruffalo
is still under contract to appear in two more

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:45.000
MCU films, although they likely won't be standalone
outings due to Universal's claim on solo movies

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.000
for the character.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.520
Still, don't go assuming you've seen the last
of the big guy yet — he's still got a few

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:51.680
fights left in him.

